# Example allowlist for claude-lumo wipe
# One project path per line (absolute or relative, as you would type it in a shell)
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# When this file exists at ~/.claude/allowlist.txt (or ~/.claude-lumo/allowlist.txt
# when CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is set), only projects OUTSIDE this list are candidates.
# Projects ON the list are never wiped automatically.
# The session-start offer hook reads this file by itself; for `claude-lumo wipe`
# pass it explicitly with --allowlist (or set WIPE_ALLOWLIST for the hook).
#
# Examples:
# C:/Users/Jim/orca/claude-lumo
# C:/Users/Jim/orca/resonia-web
# ~/.claude/projects/my-important-project
